From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the taskbar's Start button draws the Mihawk mark at every DPI

The Start button showed the Windows four-pane logo, a Microsoft trademark: at 96 DPI as sprites captured from the
prototype (patch 1140's PW_SPRITE_START and PW_SPRITE_START_HOVER), at another DPI drawn. The owner replaced it with
the project's own Mihawk mark (PS5_Proton themes/windows11/start.svg: a white squircle, an amber frame and a navy M,
original artwork), drawn by one function at every DPI (PS5_Proton src/pw_taskbar_logo.h through
wine/ps5/pw_shell_taskbar.h's pw_taskbar_logo_draw), 22 px in the 40 px button at 96 DPI where the logo was. The
button's size, place, plates and clicks are unchanged: at 96 DPI the prototype's hover and press plates go under the
mark (the hover sprite was the plate under the logo, within one level), at another DPI the taskbar's own plate. At
another DPI it replaces patch 0981's PP mark polygon, as the four panes did. Host test (tests/test_taskbar_logo.py):
librsvg's drawing of start.svg at 22, 33 and 44 px is within 1.5 levels on average.
---
diff --git a/programs/explorer/systray.c b/programs/explorer/systray.c
index 848e600..439c32d 100644
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -1068,25 +1068,9 @@ static void taskbar_paint_icon(const DRAWITEMSTRUCT *dis, struct taskbar_button
     if (!icon) icon = LoadIconW(NULL, (LPCWSTR)IDI_APPLICATION); /* Borrowed system fallback. */
     if (start)
     {
